Crowd data (public/crowd/) — data licence
=========================================

The code of this project is not licensed for reuse (all rights reserved). The data files in this
folder are a separate compilation with their own terms.

Compilation
-----------
The compilation in public/crowd/ (selection, arrangement, normalisation and the derived values
computed by scripts/crowd/build.mjs) is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

It is CC BY-NC-SA because it combines share-alike inputs (StatCounter, Firefox Public Data Report,
Appt.org) with non-commercial inputs (Cloudflare Radar, ITU data via the UN SDG database).
The project is non-commercial.

Each source keeps its own licence
---------------------------------
Numbers taken from a source remain under that source's terms; when you reuse figures from one
source, follow that source's licence and attribution line (SOURCES.md):

- World Bank WDI (population; internet use from ITU) ........ CC BY 4.0 — cite the ITU for internet use
- GeoNames ................................................ CC BY 4.0
- IANA tz database ........................................ public domain
- Eurostat (isoc_ci_dev_i, isoc_cisci_prv20) ............... reuse with acknowledgement, © European Union (CC BY 4.0)
- IBGE (SIDRA 7337) ....................................... reuse with source citation
- NTIA Internet Use Survey ................................ US government work, public domain
- StatCounter Global Stats ................................ CC BY-SA 3.0 (credit with a link to gs.statcounter.com)
- Mozilla Firefox Public Data Report ....................... CC BY-SA 3.0 or any later version (website-content licence;
                                                            the report has no separate data licence)
- Wikimedia Foundation analytics .......................... CC0 1.0
- WikiLingDiv v1.1 (Essfors) .............................. CC BY 4.0
- Unicode CLDR ............................................ Unicode License v3
- Appt.org ................................................ CC BY-SA 4.0 — a visible link to https://appt.org is required
- UN SDG Global Database / ITU ............................ UN terms of use (non-commercial, with attribution);
                                                            ITU DataHub: CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO
- Cloudflare Radar (derived cross-check shares only) ....... CC BY-NC 4.0
- Chrome Platform Status, Mozilla GLAM ..................... no explicit data licence; a few derived figures
                                                            cited with attribution
- Research papers: Gómez-Boix et al. 2018, Berke et al. 2025 (CC BY 4.0); Andriamilanto et al. 2022,
  Eckersley 2010 — individual figures cited as facts with attribution and DOI
- Cite-only single figures (DeviceAtlas, eyeo, Microsoft 2019, Wikimedia 2024) — quoted with attribution,
  not licensed for bulk reuse

Note: CC BY-SA 3.0 asks adaptations to use the same licence elements (BY-SA); combining it with
non-commercial sources is a project decision, not legal advice. If you need the StatCounter or
Firefox figures without the NC restriction, take them from the original sources.

Generated 2026-09-23 by scripts/crowd/build.mjs.
